    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a `POST`/`PUT` owner with **400** when the email domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\nFollowing the project's \"single source of truth\" convention for the email rule, I made three changes:\n\n1. **`OwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set and an `isDisposableDomain(email)` method that extracts the domain (after the `@`) and matches it case-insensitively against the blocklist. This keeps the blocklist in the one place both pipelines share.\n\n2. **`ValidateNewOwner.java`** (POST pipeline) and **`ValidateOwner.java`** (PUT pipeline) \u2014 after the existing syntactic check, each now throws the existing checked `InvalidEmailException` when the domain is blocked.\n\n`InvalidEmailException` is already wired to `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler` (returns 400 with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`), so no new escalation YAML or handler was needed. The acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full suite pass.",
